sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant W as WebhookController
    participant K as Kafka (meeting.events)
    participant MC as MeetingEventConsumer
    participant MS as MeetingService
    participant TS as TranscriptService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over C,DB: Edge case — transcript arrives AFTER meeting.ended → still stored, no data loss

    C->>W: POST meeting.ended
    W->>K: publish
    K->>MC: deliver
    MC->>MS: handleMeetingEnded
    MS->>DB: set Session ENDED (+ publish reconstruct task)

    Note over C,DB: a late transcript for the same session arrives afterwards
    C->>W: POST meeting.transcript (late, seq=N+1)
    W->>K: publish
    W-->>C: 202 Accepted
    K->>MC: deliver
    MC->>TS: handleTranscript
    TS->>DB: session exists → insert segment
    Note right of TS: Session stays ENDED. Segment is persisted and<br/>visible via GET, but the already-written file is<br/>NOT auto-reassembled (re-reconstruction is a future hook)
